course: dictionary
lesson: 13352
title: Hamstring: a muscle and a doing word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Your hamstrings are strong muscles and tendons at the back of your thigh, just above your knee. They work hard when you run, jump or kick. «Sam pulled a hamstring during the football match and had to sit out.» The words pulled and sit out are the clues: a hamstring that is hurt makes you stop playing.
explain: Hamstring can also be a doing word. It means to stop someone or something from working well. «The club was hamstrung by a lack of money, so the new pitch had to wait.» The clue is lack of money: the club could not do what it wanted, so its plans were held back.
explain: Context tells you which meaning to use. In a PE lesson, hamstring names a part of the body. In a news report about plans, it describes something being held back. Check by swapping in «held back» or «stopped from working well» and seeing if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A hamstring (noun) is one of the strong tendons or muscles at the back of the thigh, above the knee.
fact: To hamstring (verb) means to stop someone or something from working well.
fact: «Hamstrung» is the past form: «The team was hamstrung by injuries.»
fact: Stretching your hamstrings is a common warm-up before sport.
fact: A very old meaning of hamstring (verb) is to cut an animal's hamstring so it cannot run.
exercise: «Mia stretched her hamstrings before the race.» Where are the hamstrings? | On the top of the head | *At the back of the thigh, above the knee | In the stomach | On the palm of the hand
exercise: «The club was hamstrung by a lack of money.» What does hamstrung mean here? | Cheered loudly | Made very rich | *Held back and stopped from working well
exercise: Ravi says, «I pulled a hamstring playing rugby.» What has happened to Ravi? | *He hurt the muscle at the back of his thigh | He fell asleep | He won a race | He tore his shirt
test: «The coach said to do a hamstring stretch before running.» What is a hamstring stretch? | *A stretch for the muscles at the back of the thigh | Lying on your back and yawning | Dancing on one leg | Jumping as high as you can
test: «Our plans were hamstrung because the new rules changed.» What does hamstrung mean? | *Stopped from working well | Put in a box | Made much bigger | Painted in bright colours
exam: Which sentence uses hamstring as a verb, meaning to stop something working well? | «He stretched his hamstring slowly before the race.» | *«The new rules hamstrung the school's plans.» | «The hamstring is at the back of the leg.» | «Lia's hamstring feels sore after football.»
